<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    TrayFlyoutWindow — the Acrylic 360x540 flyout shown on a single-click of the tray icon
    (UI-SPEC §Component Inventory TrayHost row + §Interaction Contracts Tray). This is a thin
    Window: the SystemBackdrop (DesktopAcrylicBackdrop, UI-SPEC §Design System) + chrome removal
    live here, while all the bound content (header, drives list, recent activity, footer) lives
    in the FrameworkElement-rooted TrayFlyoutView UserControl set as Content in code-behind.

    Why the split (Rule-3 deviation, see 17-11-SUMMARY): WinUI 3 forbids {x:Bind} on a <Window>
    root — Window is not a FrameworkElement, so the compiled-bindings code-gen fails (CS1503).
    Moving the {x:Bind} surface into a UserControl is the standard WinUI 3 pattern.
    Port of TrayMenuView.swift.
-->
<Window
    x:Class="DS3Drive.App.Tray.TrayFlyoutWindow"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:tray="using:DS3Drive.App.Tray">

    <!-- Flyout size: Width="360" Height="540" (UI-SPEC Open Q #2 default). The Window is sized
         to these via AppWindow.Resize in code-behind; the host grid carries them as its content
         footprint so the hosted TrayFlyoutView lays out at the intended 360x540. -->
    <Grid x:Name="HostGrid" Width="360" Height="540" />
</Window>
